1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wencheng_of_Northern_Wei
2 CONT
2 CONT Emperor Wencheng of Northern Wei
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Chinese Emperor Emperor Wencheng of Northern Wei Birth and death Birth date	440[1] Death date	June 20, 465[2][3] Names Family name	Tuòbá (拓拔) Given name	Jùn (濬) Reign Dates of reign (1st)	Octo
2 CONC ber 31, 452[4][3]–June 20, 465 Dynasty	Northern Wei Era name	Xīng'ān (興安) (452-454) Xīngguāng (興光) (454-455) Tài'ān (太安) (455-459) Hépíng (和平) (460-465) Temple name	Gāozōng (高宗) Posthumous name: (full)	Emperor Wénchéng (文成皇帝, "civ
2 CONC il and successful")
2 CONT
2 CONT Emperor Wencheng of Northern Wei ((北)魏文成帝) (440–465), personal name Tuoba Jun (拓拔濬), was an emperor of the Xianbei dynasty Northern Wei. He became emperor in the aftermaths of the eunuch Zong Ai's assassination of his grandfather 
2 CONC Emperor Taiwu and uncle Tuoba Yu, and he was generally described by historians as a ruler who sought foremost to allow his people to rest after his grandfather's expansionist policies and extensive campaigns, who also reformed the
2 CONC  laws to become more lenient.
