1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juvansher '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Javanshir, also known by his Middle Persian name Juvansher (meaning young lion) was the son of Khosrau II, and Gordiya, the sister of Bahram Chobin. Not much is known about him.
2 CONT
2 CONT [...at the start of the 7th century, the Mihranid dynasty, in origin Persian, established itself in Utik, then seized Artsakh and held them for about two centuries,]...[In the beginning, they controlled only the the lone canton of
2 CONC  Gardman (in Utik). Under Varaz Grigor (626-637) and under Jivanshir (637-683), they took control of the Armenian portion of Albania and then of all the old marzpanate and recognized the authority of the Caliph.]... ref: page 59 o
