2 CONT
2 CONT * Wilaadat (Birth): 
2 CONT * Wafaat (Death): 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr Arabic: محمد بن أبي بكر‎ was the son of Abu Bakr, a companion of the Islamic prophet Muhammad and first Rashidun Caliph. His mother was Asma bint Umays. He became the adopted son of the first Imam, and fourth
2 CONC  Rashidun caliph, Ali ibn Abi Talib and became one of his generals
2 CONT
2 CONT The Shi'a praise Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr for his devotion to `Ali and his resistance to all the other caliphs who the Shi'a believe to be usurpers. Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr was a pious Muslim who supported the Imam of his time, Ali ibn
2 CONC  Abi Talib, even though his sister Aisha opposed `Ali in the battle of Jamal, Ibn Abu Bakr was faithful to his stepfather. And he was in Ali's army in the Battle of Jamal and later it was Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr who escorted Aisha b
2 CONC ack to Madina. According to a Shi'a Muslim author: `Ali loved Muhammad Ibn Abu Bakr as his own son and his death was felt as another terrible shock. `Ali prayed for him, and invoked God's blessings and mercy upon his soul.[6] His 
2 CONC tomb is located in a mosque in Cairo, Egypt.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From ''Banu Taym'' Tribe (Part of ''Banu Quraysh'' Tribe).
